  "id": "Compound::DB00697 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Tizanidine is likely to interact with Adra2c through a shared pathway involving Adra2b. The evidence suggests that Tizanidine binds to Adra2b, which then participates in various receptor activities, including Alpha2-adrenergic and Alpha-adrenergic receptor functions. These activities are ultimately participated by Adra2c, indicating a potential functional link between Tizanidine and Adra2c. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Tizanidine influences Adra2c, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for Adra2b as a bridge between Tizanidine and Adra2c, emphasizing the importance of receptor activity in mediating this relationship.",
